id: pm-csv-9jj1
title: "Full-cycle hardening wave: pm-csv"
description: "Track dependency, changelog, release checks, and security hardening evidence."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: deps-2026-6-7,full-cycle-hardening,hardening-pass,wave-full-cycle-2026-06-07
created_at: "2026-06-07T07:41:34.875Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:23:54.868Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:23:54.868Z"
author: codex-5.3-full-cycle
release: 2026.6.8
resolution: "Work completed and released in 2026.6.8. Release attribution set explicitly so pm-changelog --respect-item-release files the entry under 2026.6.8, the first release that actually contains the implementing merge c9060ed. An earlier revision of this record said 2026.6.7; that was wrong, because v2026.06.07 was tagged at 07:15:36Z and the merge landed at 08:12Z."
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.6.8 heading, the first release whose tree contains the hardening-wave merge, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Before this closeout the item had remained in_progress with no activity since its work shipped, so the delivery was missing from the changelog while still counting as open work in every fleet audit. A first attempt then filed it under 2026.6.7, a release cut before the work landed and therefore unable to contain it."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-06-07T07:41:36.337Z",codex-5.3-full-cycle,"Hardening pass complete: release:check succeeded after dependency bump and changelog regeneration."
  "2026-06-07T08:00:41.688Z",codex-5.3-full-cycle,"Security gate: high-confidence token/key regex scan over tracked files and git history found no actionable secrets. Binary-history false positives were traced to embedded wasm base64 blobs, not credentials."
  "2026-07-27T23:21:15.887Z",claude-code,"Release attribution corrected from 2026.6.7 to 2026.6.8. The original value came from mapping the item's last-activity DATE to a same-day release, which is unsound to the hour: v2026.06.07 was tagged at 07:15:36Z and the implementing merge c9060ed landed at 08:12Z, so the 2026.6.7 release provably does NOT contain this work. Verified by containment rather than dates - git merge-base --is-ancestor c9060ed v2026.06.07 fails while v2026.06.08 succeeds, making v2026.06.08 the first release that actually carried it. Greptile surfaced this class of error on the sibling pm-web PR #67 by spotting a historical release predating its implementation."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  CHANGELOG.md,project,Regenerated changelog to satisfy release gate
  package-lock.json,project,Regenerated lockfile after dependency alignment
  package.json,project,Upgraded @unbrained/pm-cli and pm-changelog to latest ranges
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "npm run release:check",.,project,2400
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  README.md,project,Primary package docs reference
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the full-cycle hardening wave for pm-csv was completed and released in 2026.6.8, verified by containment (git merge-base --is-ancestor c9060ed v2026.06.08 succeeds while v2026.06.07 fails). The item was never closed and sat in progress for seven weeks, inflating every fleet audit."
body: Master execution item for full-cycle hardening in pm-csv.
